      "message": "This is weird and I am not 100% happy with this.  I tried to explore alternatives in https://docs.google.com/document/d/1EPn1Ss-hfOC6Ki_B5CC6GA_UFnY3TmoDLCP2HjP7bms/edit#heading\u003dh.anqc8fi2lnkn\n\nBut yes, the caller is on the C++ side which means that:\n\n* They can\u0027t move/pass `self` by value (this is not supported by `cxx`-based FFI;  Crubit-based FFI will support this)\n* And since we need to work with `\u0026mut self`, we need to leave it in a state that\u0027s valid for C++.",
